course: dictionary
lesson: 449
title: Argon, a gas in the air
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scientists use context to understand new words, just as you do in English. «Air is a mixture of gases: about four fifths is nitrogen, about one fifth is oxygen, and the rest is a little argon...» The word mixture tells you the air is made of several different things, and the words «a little» tell you that argon is only a small part of it.
explain: Argon is a gas you cannot see, smell or taste, so you would never notice it in the air. Its name is hidden in the sentence, but you can work out its job by checking the clues: argon is one of the gases that make up air, and it is found in a small amount.
explain: Argon is a noble gas. This means it hardly ever reacts with other substances, so it does not burn or change easily. That is why it is useful in some light bulbs and in welding. A quick check: swap in your own meaning and see whether the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Argon is a gas with no colour, no smell and no taste.
fact: Argon is found in small amounts in the air.
fact: «Argon» is a chemical element, and its symbol is Ar.
fact: «Noble gas» means a gas that hardly ever reacts with other substances.
fact: Argon is used inside some light bulbs and in welding because it does not burn or react.
exercise: «...and the rest is a little argon...» What does «a little argon» suggest about how much argon is in air? | Argon is a liquid | Argon is most of the air | A huge amount, more than the oxygen | *A small amount
exercise: Argon is called a noble gas. What does noble gas mean? | A gas that smells very strong | A gas that is always hot | *A gas that hardly ever reacts with other substances | A solid that melts easily
exercise: On the periodic table, argon has a chemical symbol. Find and copy it. | *Ar | Ap | Ag | Au
test: Why is argon used inside some light bulbs? | *Because it does not burn or react | Because it is a metal that shines | Because it smells sweet | Because it burns brightly
test: Argon has no colour, no smell and no taste. What does this tell you? | *You cannot see, smell or taste it in the air | You can see it glowing red | It smells of flowers | It tastes sour like a lemon
exam: Which statement about argon is true? | Argon is the main gas in air | *Argon is a gas found in small amounts in air | Argon burns quickly when heated | Argon is a solid metal that rusts easily
